<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Pre-Islamic Mecca</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 630 CE (approx.) · capital Mecca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The sanctuary town of the Kaaba, governed by the clans of Quraysh, whose trade and pilgrimage made it the birthplace of Islam.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Arab tradition credits <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qusayy-ibn-kilab">Qusayy ibn Kilab</a> with gathering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> clans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in the 5th century and taking control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a>, a shrine already visited by pilgrims from across western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. He distributed the hereditary offices of the sanctuary: guarding the Kaaba, giving water and food to pilgrims and holding the war banner.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> had no king. Clans such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hashim">Hashim</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-makhzum">Makhzum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-umayya">Umayya</a> and Abd al-Dar shared power through an assembly of elders. The town lived on the pilgrimage, the sacred months that protected trade, nearby fairs such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souq-ukaz">Ukaz</a> and caravans to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> housed images of many deities, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubal">Hubal</a> chief among them, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> was recognised as a high god.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Muhammad, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hashim">clan of Hashim</a>, began preaching around 610, met growing opposition and left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> in 622. After years of war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> surrendered to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-state-of-medina">Islamic state of Medina</a> in 630; the idols of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> were destroyed and the town became the holiest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 450 CE – 630 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.66%;width:3.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 630 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mecca</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Qusayy ibn Kilab, Abd al-Muttalib, Abu Sufyan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arabian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mecca under the Quraysh, Quraysh of Mecca</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=540&amp;focus=pre-islamic-mecca" aria-label="Pre-Islamic Mecca on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5750 1386 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pre-Islamic Mecca lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6070 1642L6053 1533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6053 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6070 1642h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6070 1642h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mecca. <a href="/atlas?year=540&amp;focus=pre-islamic-mecca">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

